+   "source": [
+    "import numpy as np\n",
+    "import gtsam\n",
+    "import plotly.graph_objects as go\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "8ea56ff8",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Create a 3D synthetic localization problem\n",
+    "\n",
+    "We choose one true 3D point and four fixed landmarks. The landmarks are spread through space so that the resulting range measurements provide independent geometric constraints.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Gaussian noise is added to each raw range measurement for realism."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 24,
+   "id": "df3990e8",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stdout",
+     "output_type": "stream",
+     "text": [
+      "True point: [1. 2. 3.]\n",
+      "Raw range standard deviation: 0.100 m\n",
+      "\n",
+      "L0: [0. 0. 0.] True range = 3.742 m,  Measured range = 3.772 m\n",
+      "L1: [5. 0. 0.] True range = 5.385 m,  Measured range = 5.281 m\n",
+      "L2: [0. 6. 0.] True range = 5.099 m,  Measured range = 5.174 m\n",
+      "L3: [1. 0. 8.] True range = 5.385 m,  Measured range = 5.479 m\n"
+     ]
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "rng = np.random.default_rng(42)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "x_true = np.array([1.0, 2.0, 3.0])\n",
+    "\n",
+    "landmarks = np.array([\n",
+    "    [0.0, 0.0, 0.0],\n",
+    "    [5.0, 0.0, 0.0],\n",
+    "    [0.0, 6.0, 0.0],\n",
+    "    [1.0, 0.0, 8.0],\n",
+    "])\n",
+    "\n",
+    "range_sigma = 0.10  # raw range standard deviation [m]\n",
+    "\n",
+    "true_ranges = [np.linalg.norm(x_true - wL) for wL in landmarks]\n",
+    "\n",
+    "measurement_noise = rng.normal(\n",
+    "    loc=0.0, scale=range_sigma, size=len(landmarks)\n",
+    ")\n",
+    "\n",
+    "measured_ranges = true_ranges + measurement_noise\n",
+    "\n",
+    "print(\"True point:\", x_true)\n",
+    "print(f\"Raw range standard deviation: {range_sigma:.3f} m\\n\")\n",
+    "\n",
+    "for i, (wL, r_true, r_measured) in enumerate(\n",
+    "    zip(landmarks, true_ranges, measured_ranges)):\n",
+    "    print(\n",
+    "        f\"L{i}: {wL} \"\n",
+    "        f\"True range = {r_true:.3f} m, \",\n",
+    "        f\"Measured range = {r_measured:.3f} m\"\n",
+    "    )"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "5934ab25",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Propagate range uncertainty into squared-range units\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The sensor uncertainty above is expressed in range units, while `KnownLandmarkSquaredRangeFactor3` uses the squared-range residual\n",
+    "\n",
+    "$$\n",
+    "e_i(x) = \\|x - L_i\\|^2 - d_i^2.\n",
+    "$$\n",
+    "\n",
+    "For $y = d^2$, first-order uncertainty propagation gives\n",
+    "\n",
+    "$$\n",
+    "\\sigma_y \\approx \\left|\\frac{\\partial d^2}{\\partial d}\\right|\\sigma_d = 2d\\,\\sigma_d.\n",
+    "$$\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Therefore, the standard deviation used by each factor is approximately\n",
+    "\n",
+    "$$\n",
+    "\\sigma_{d^2} \\approx 2d\\,\\sigma_d.\n",
+    "$$\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Even when each range measurement has the same $\\sigma_d$, their respective squared-range uncertainties differ between landmarks."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "ee258de2",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Build the factor graph\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Each range measurement contributes one factor to the same unknown point state."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 25,
+   "id": "f48e207c",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "key = 0\n",
+    "graph = gtsam.NonlinearFactorGraph()\n",
+    "\n",
+    "for wL, measured_range in zip(landmarks, measured_ranges):\n",
+    "    sigma_squared_range = 2.0 * measured_range * range_sigma\n",
+    "    model = gtsam.noiseModel.Isotropic.Sigma(1, sigma_squared_range)\n",
+    "    graph.add(\n",
+    "        gtsam.KnownLandmarkSquaredRangeFactor3(key, wL, measured_range, model)\n",
+    "    )"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "eb81f04e",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Choose an initial estimate\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The nonlinear optimizer needs an initial value for the point state. The initial position is deliberately offset from the true position."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 26,
+   "id": "a64e0da3",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "x_initial = np.array([1.2, 1.7, 3.2])\n",
+    "\n",
+    "initial = gtsam.Values()\n",
+    "initial.insert(key, x_initial)"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "cdb7d696",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Optimize\n",
+    "\n",
+    "We solve the nonlinear least-squares problem with Levenberg-Marquardt."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 27,
+   "id": "fa84a534",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stdout",
+     "output_type": "stream",
+     "text": [
+      "True point:  [1. 2. 3.]\n",
+      "Initial point:  [1.2 1.7 3.2]\n",
+      "Estimated point:  [1.14882058 1.99174407 2.96859758]\n",
+      "Final graph error:  0.41722601045710256\n",
+      "Localization error:  0.15232149470799192\n"
+     ]
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "optimizer = gtsam.LevenbergMarquardtOptimizer(graph, initial)\n",
+    "result = optimizer.optimize()\n",
+    "\n",
+    "x_estimated = result.atVector(key)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "print(\"True point: \", x_true)\n",
+    "print(\"Initial point: \", x_initial)\n",
+    "print(\"Estimated point: \", x_estimated)\n",
+    "print(\"Final graph error: \", graph.error(result))\n",
+    "print(\"Localization error: \", np.linalg.norm(x_estimated - x_true))"
+   ]
